---
import FullNavigationLayout from "../../astro/layouts/FullNavigationLayout.astro";

const stackExample = `<section class="mr-stack">...</section>`;
const clusterExample = `<div class="mr-cluster mr-cluster--between">...</div>`;
const inlineExample = `<span class="mr-inline">...</span>`;
const gridExample = `<section class="mr-grid">...</section>`;
const containerExample = `<main class="mr-container">...</main>`;
---

<FullNavigationLayout>
  <main class="mr-container mr-shell__main">
    <h1>Layout primitives</h1>
    <p>
      Markup Refine keeps layout deliberately small and intrinsic instead of
      reproducing an atomic utility framework.
    </p>

    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <p>Vertical flow with <code>--mr-stack-gap</code>.</p>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{stackExample}</code></pre>

    <h2>Cluster</h2>
    <p>Wrapping horizontal grouping with optional repeated-use alignment modifiers.</p>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{clusterExample}</code></pre>

    <h2>Inline</h2>
    <p>
      An inline-level layout group. Use semantic inline elements directly when no
      layout group is needed.
    </p>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{inlineExample}</code></pre>

    <h2>Grid</h2>
    <p>
      Intrinsic auto-fit columns controlled by <code>--mr-grid-min-column-size</code>
      and <code>--mr-grid-gap</code>.
    </p>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{gridExample}</code></pre>

    <h2>Container</h2>
    <p>Bounded inline size with fluid padding and no dedicated mobile breakpoint.</p>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{containerExample}</code></pre>

    <h2>Admission rule</h2>
    <p>
      A new general primitive must solve a repeated layout relationship that the
      existing five cannot express cleanly without creating an atomic property or
      breakpoint catalog.
    </p>
  </main>
</FullNavigationLayout>
